.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH orbit-add 1  "add " 
.SH NAME
orbit\-add \- Add a task. Quick\-add syntax applies: dates, p1\-p4, #label, @Area or @project
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit add\fR [\fB\-\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITITLE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a task. Quick\-add syntax applies: dates, p1\-p4, #label, @Area or @project
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Use this UUID for the task. Adding an id that exists is a no\-op
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON object per result, with `"v":1`, instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fITITLE\fR>

.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  orbit add "buy milk"
  orbit add call the dentist tomorrow 9am p2 #health
  orbit add \-\-id 3f2b9c1e\-6d4a\-4b8e\-9f1a\-2c7d5e8b0a11 "buy milk" \-\-dry\-run
